  "mechanismSummary": "Ozonolysis has cut the cyclopentene of Johnson's tetracycle into a methyl ketone and a B-ring ketone, five bonds apart. Hydroxide forms the methyl ketone enolate, which attacks the B-ring carbonyl and closes a six-membered ring, the aldol step of a Robinson annulation. The alkoxide is protonated, a second enolate forms, and hydroxide leaves by E1cB to give the conjugated cyclohexenone: ring A of progesterone. The five-membered initiator ring has become the six-membered A ring, with the angular methyl group it carried in place. The acetyl ketone on the D ring could also enolise, but its enolate cannot reach another carbonyl. The stereocentres made in the cascade are not touched, so the product is (racemic) progesterone; the app does not check stereochemistry yet.",
